            <title>Setup Github pages as your blog</title>
            <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/setup-github-pages-as-your-blog/</link>
            <pubDate>Sat, 10 Sep 2016 00:00:00 +0700</pubDate>
            <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/setup-github-pages-as-your-blog/</guid>
            <description>&lt;p&gt;How to setup github page as your blog? It&amp;rsquo;s actually very easy, just follow the following guides&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://24ways.org/2013/get-started-with-github-pages/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;Get Started With GitHub Pages (Plus Bonus Jekyll)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://www.thinkful.com/learn/a-guide-to-using-github-pages/start/new-project/user-page/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;A guide to using Github Pages&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://knightlab.northwestern.edu/2013/06/13/getting-github-why-journalists-should-know-and-use-the-social-coding-site/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;Getting GitHub: Why journalists should know and use the social coding site&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/csswizardry/csswizardry.github.com&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;csswizardry.github.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;</description>
        </item><item>
            <title>Embed git file to pelican</title>
            <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/embed-git-file-to-pelican/</link>
            <pubDate>Thu, 11 Sep 2014 00:00:00 +0700</pubDate>
            <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/embed-git-file-to-pelican/</guid>
            <description>&lt;p&gt;Writing articles in github pages is nice, because you have github repository with all the nice features for document management, however sometimes it&amp;rsquo;s not where I want my articles to reside. For instance, I want the articles about git to be in a separate &lt;code&gt;git&lt;/code&gt; repository.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have several solutions for this problem:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;I could duplicate the article. But I won&amp;rsquo;t do this.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;I could store the articles as &lt;code&gt;gist&lt;/code&gt; like this:&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;[gist:id=dc8b7c536d0fe9c7003f]&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But I can&amp;rsquo;t store a lot of related things in gist because that&amp;rsquo;s the role of a real git repo.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;I could store the articles in the normal &lt;code&gt;git&lt;/code&gt; repo, and embed it into the article in github page. I chose this approach for long articles. Like this:&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;!-- &lt;script src=&#34;http://gistit-minhhh.appspot.com/github/robertkrimen/gist-it-example/blob/master/example.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt; --&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There&amp;rsquo;s already a nice tool to do this: &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/minhhh/gist-it&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;gist-it&lt;/a&gt;. Using it is really simple, just clone the repo and deploy it to an AppEngine instance. The downside of this is it does not generate &lt;code&gt;html&lt;/code&gt; code for &lt;code&gt;Markdown&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The best solution for me is to use a plugin for embedding git file into &lt;code&gt;pelican&lt;/code&gt; like this:&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/minhhh/wiki&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;minhhh/wiki/sample.md&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;</description>
        </item><item>
            <title>Creating this blog</title>
            <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/creating-this-blog/</link>
            <pubDate>Sat, 07 Jun 2014 00:00:00 +0700</pubDate>
            <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/creating-this-blog/</guid>
            <description>&lt;p&gt;When creating this blog, I used the following references:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://ntanjerome.org/blog/how-to-setup-github-user-page-with-pelican&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;Setup github page with pelican&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://mathamy.com/migrating-to-github-pages-using-pelican.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;Migrating to github pages&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://www.macdrifter.com/2012/08/pelican-guide-moving-from-wordpress-and-initial-setup.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;Pelican Guide initial setup&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://www.macdrifter.com/2012/08/moving-to-pelican-design-planning.html&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;Moving to Pelican planning&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/streeter/pelican-gist&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;pelican-gist&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/minhhh/gist-it&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&#xA;    &gt;gist-it&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;</description>
        </item></channel>
